Fix the dead fling: don't coalesce wheel events across scrolling phases on WPE.

Root cause, device-traced on franceinfo.fr (WEBKIT_FLINGVEL_LOG=1):

  [flingvel] COALESCE 9 events -> 1 ... mergedDelta=0.0,-660.0
  [kinetic]  wheel in: delta=0.0,-660.0 ... endOfNonMomentum=1 historySize=0
  [flingvel] SINGLE-SAMPLE samples=1 motion=1 span=0ms -> velocity 0,0 (NO MOMENTUM)

The WPE touch gesture recogniser emits a flick as N Changed-phase motion events
followed by one Ended-phase event (zero delta) that marks the gesture boundary
the kinetic fling arms from. WebWheelEventCoalescer::canCoalesce() gates its
phase-equality check to PLATFORM(COCOA), so on WPE nothing stops the Ended event
from merging into the motion stream. When the WebProcess is slow to ack - i.e.
on a heavy page - the queue fills and the coalescer merges the ENTIRE gesture,
motion events and the Ended event alike, into a single wheel event that carries
the summed delta and Phase::Ended. ScrollingEffectsController then sees one
sample at gesture end: zero time span, zero velocity, no fling. The page stops
dead under the finger.

This is why the defect only appears on busy sites and never reproduced on a
trivial local page: coalescing only engages when events queue behind an
un-acked WebProcess, which a light page never causes. It also explains the
milder half-speed flings (a partial merge leaves two samples ~140ms apart) and
why the earlier hypotheses missed - the loss is neither in touch delivery
(measured in==out) nor in the estimator, but in phase-blind coalescing between
the two.

Fix: apply the existing phase-inequality guard on WPE/GTK/libwpe, not just
Cocoa. phase() is carried on all these ports (canCoalesce already reads it in
the Cocoa arm and coalesce() reads it in the libwpe arm). Motion and Ended
events now stay distinct, so the full motion history reaches the fling.
WEBKIT_WHEEL_COALESCE_PHASE_SPLIT=0 restores the upstream Cocoa-only behaviour.

Supersedes the single-sample fallback mitigation, which should now stay off:
with the history intact there is no lone sample to rescue.

Must apply AFTER webkit-flingvel-log-diagnostic.patch (shares the file's
added includes).

diff -ruN a/Source/WebKit/Shared/WebWheelEventCoalescer.cpp b/Source/WebKit/Shared/WebWheelEventCoalescer.cpp
--- a/Source/WebKit/Shared/WebWheelEventCoalescer.cpp	2026-07-20 20:37:12.237498225 +0000
+++ b/Source/WebKit/Shared/WebWheelEventCoalescer.cpp	2026-07-20 20:37:36.821653050 +0000
@@ -47,6 +47,17 @@
     return enabled;
 }
 
+// Whether events in different scrolling phases are kept from coalescing on non-Cocoa
+// ports. On by default (the fix); WEBKIT_WHEEL_COALESCE_PHASE_SPLIT=0 restores stock.
+static bool wheelCoalescePhaseSplitEnabled()
+{
+    static bool enabled = [] {
+        const char* v = getenv("WEBKIT_WHEEL_COALESCE_PHASE_SPLIT");
+        return !v || (*v && *v != '0');
+    }();
+    return enabled;
+}
+
 // Represents the number of wheel events we can hold in the queue before we start pushing them preemptively.
 constexpr unsigned wheelEventQueueSizeThreshold = 10;
 
@@ -70,9 +81,21 @@
         return false;
     if (a.granularity() != b.granularity())
         return false;
-#if PLATFORM(COCOA)
-    if (a.phase() != b.phase())
+#if PLATFORM(COCOA) || PLATFORM(GTK) || USE(LIBWPE) || ENABLE(WPE_PLATFORM)
+    // Events in different scrolling phases must never coalesce. On WPE the touch
+    // gesture recogniser emits Changed-phase motion events and a final Ended-phase
+    // event (zero delta) that marks the gesture boundary the kinetic fling is armed
+    // from. Upstream gates this check to Cocoa, so on WPE a whole flick's motion
+    // events plus the Ended event merged into ONE event carrying the merged delta and
+    // Phase::Ended — the fling then saw a single sample, zero time span, and computed
+    // zero velocity, so busy pages (franceinfo.fr) stopped dead under the finger
+    // instead of coasting. Device-traced: "COALESCE 9 events -> 1 ... endOfNonMomentum=1
+    // historySize=0". phase() is carried on all these ports, so apply the guard here.
+    // WEBKIT_WHEEL_COALESCE_PHASE_SPLIT=0 restores the upstream (Cocoa-only) behaviour.
+    if (wheelCoalescePhaseSplitEnabled() && a.phase() != b.phase())
         return false;
+#endif
+#if PLATFORM(COCOA)
     if (a.momentumPhase() != b.momentumPhase())
         return false;
 #endif
